,\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The average amount of data written to disk or other\\nblock device, calculated over the last minute.\\n\\nThis object has been deprecated in favour of\\n\'ssIORawSent(57)\', which can be used to calculate\\nthe same metric, but over any desired time period.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssIOSent\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.5\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"deprecated\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The average amount of data read from disk or other\\nblock device, calculated over the last minute.\\n\\nThis object has been deprecated in favour of\\n\'ssIORawReceived(58)\', which can be used to calculate\\nthe same metric, but over any desired time period.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssIOReceive\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.6\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"deprecated\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The average rate of interrupts processed (including\\nthe clock) calculated over the last minute.\\n\\nThis object has been deprecated in favour of\\n\'ssRawInterrupts(59)\', which can be used to calculate\\nthe same metric, but over any desired time period.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssSysInterrupts\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.7\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"deprecated\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The average rate of context switches,\\ncalculated over the last minute.\\n\\nThis object has been deprecated in favour of\\n\'ssRawContext(60)\', which can be used to calculate\\nthe same metric, but over any desired time period.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssSysContext\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.8\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"deprecated\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The percentage of CPU time spent processing\\nuser-level code, calculated over the last minute.\\n\\nThis object has been deprecated in favour of\\n\'ssCpuRawUser(50)\', which can be used to calculate\\nthe same metric, but over any desired time period.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuUser\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.9\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"deprecated\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The percentage of CPU time spent processing\\nsystem-level code, calculated over the last minute.\\n\\nThis object has been deprecated in favour of\\n\'ssCpuRawSystem(52)\', which can be used to calculate\\nthe same metric, but over any desired time period.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuSystem\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.10\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"deprecated\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The percentage of processor time spent idle,\\ncalculated over the last minute.\\n\\nThis object has been deprecated in favour of\\n\'ssCpuRawIdle(53)\', which can be used to calculate\\nthe same metric, but over any desired time period.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuIdle\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.11\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"deprecated\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nprocessing user-level code.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawUser\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.50\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nprocessing reduced-priority code.\\n\\nThis object will not be implemented on hosts where\\nthe underlying operating system does not measure\\nthis particular CPU metric.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawNice\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.51\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nprocessing system-level code.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\\n\\nThis object may sometimes be implemented as the\\ncombination of the \'ssCpuRawWait(54)\' and\\n\'ssCpuRawKernel(55)\' counters, so care must be\\ntaken when summing the overall raw counters.\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawSystem\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.52\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nidle.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawIdle\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.53\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nwaiting for IO.\\n\\nThis object will not be implemented on hosts where\\nthe underlying operating system does not measure\\nthis particular CPU metric.  This time may also be\\nincluded within the \'ssCpuRawSystem(52)\' counter.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawWait\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.54\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nprocessing kernel-level code.\\n\\nThis object will not be implemented on hosts where\\nthe underlying operating system does not measure\\nthis particular CPU metric.  This time may also be\\nincluded within the \'ssCpuRawSystem(52)\' counter.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawKernel\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.55\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nprocessing hardware interrupts.\\n\\nThis object will not be implemented on hosts where\\nthe underlying operating system does not measure\\nthis particular CPU metric.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawInterrupt\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.56\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"Number of blocks sent to a block device\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssIORawSent\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.57\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"Number of blocks received from a block device\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssIORawReceived\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.58\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"Number of interrupts processed\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssRawInterrupts\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.59\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"Number of context switches\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssRawContexts\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.60\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nprocessing software interrupts.\\n\\nThis object will not be implemented on hosts where\\nthe underlying operating system does not measure\\nthis particular CPU metric.\\n\\nOn a multi-processor system, the \'ssCpuRaw*\'\\ncounters are cumulative over all CPUs, so their\\nsum will typically be N*100 (for N processors).\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssCpuRawSoftIRQ\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.61\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"Number of blocks swapped in\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssRawSwapIn\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.62\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"Number of blocks swapped out\",\"index\":[],\"name\":\"ssRawSwapOut\",\"objectID\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11.63\",\"pid\":\"1.3.6.1.4.1.2021.11\",\"status\":\"current\",\"subTree\":[],\"syntax\":\"INTEGER\",\"type\":\"OBJECT\"},{\"access\":\"read-only\",\"description\":\"The number of \'ticks\' (typically 1/100s) spent\\nby the hyper